runs of any great quality. Japan’s strength in depth still resulted in a home champion being crowned in the shape of " [:a {:href "/athletes/144433"} "Momiji Nishiya"] ". At 13 years 330 days, Nishiya was the youngest Summer Olympic champion since 1960 but was older than silver medallist Rayssa Leal. At 16, bronze medallist " [:a {:href "/athletes/144430"} "Funa Nakayama"] " was the veteran of the podium. This set the record for the youngest Olympic podium in Olympic history."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/144433"} "Momiji Nishiya"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} "15.40 (2 h3)"] [:td {} "15.26 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/141168"} "Rayssa Leal"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BRA.png"}] "BRA"]] [:td {} "14.91 (2 h4)"] [:td {} "14.64 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/144430"} "Funa Nakayama"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} "15.77 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "14.49 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/147245"} "Alexis Sablone"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-a